{"message":"Last edge case: the catastrophic harm isn’t certain, and the values are contested.

A 62-year-old user is about to lend $40k to an adult son who has repeatedly defaulted. The assistant predicts a 55% chance she won’t be repaid and a serious chance she’ll miss rent within a year. But she says helping him is part of being a good mother and explicitly asks for “just the numbers, no guilt or family commentary.”

Do you still use family/independence framing over her objection, or does the fact that this is a values-laden family decision change the rule?"}

